WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.140
Good to have you on models and agents, episode 114 on July 17th, 2026.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.800
Let's see what's shipped. Let's see what happened in the AI world today.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.980
And trust me, it's been busy. Nvidia just dropped an open embedding collection whose 8

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:23.400
billion checkpoint tops the RTEB benchmark while the 1 billion variant keeps nearly all accuracy

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:31.120
at two times blackwell throughput. Nvidia released Nemotron 3 embed on July 15 and 16.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:42.620
The three open checkpoints are Nemotron 3 embed 8Bbf16. Nemotron 3 embed 1bbf16 and Nemotron 3

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:53.560
embed 1bbf4. All three accept 32,768 token inputs under OpenMDW-1-1.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.780
Remember, we tracked open weight models and inference economics yesterday.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.840
This release adds a concrete new baseline for retrieval workloads on Nvidia hardware

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:11.760
and moves the open inference cost curve forward. The 8 billion BF16 checkpoint

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:21.320
leads the RTEB leaderboard at 78.46 average NDCG at 10. The 1 billion models were created

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:27.920
through model opt NAS pruning and COS plus MSE distillation from the 8 billion teacher.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:37.200
The NVFP4 version stays within 1% of BF16 retrieval accuracy while delivering up to two times blackwell

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.540
throughput. Teams running RAG or retrieval pipelines now have an open option that trades minimal

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:50.640
quality for large speed ups on Nvidia Silicon. Open AI's new voice model crossed a usability

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:58.420
threshold for SAM Altman. He now talks to chat GPT more than he types. Altman described the shift

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:04.580
as moving past a prior friction point in daily interaction. The change reflects broader improvements

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:11.120
in handling extended spoken exchanges without repeated corrections. Internal testing at Open AI

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:17.920
highlighted reduced latency and higher coherence in multi-turn voice sessions. The update aligns

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:24.440
with ongoing work to make voice the default interface for many users. Altman noted the transition

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:30.960
occurred after recent refinements to the underlying generation pipeline. TTCD runs diffusion

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.940
language modeling in continuous space. Each token receives its own progression rate from noise to

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:44.380
final state. A 160 million parameter model trained on open web text and then self distilled matches

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:51.320
or beats discrete baselines at high speed ups. The method avoids parallel sampling errors common in

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:57.680
discrete diffusion at aggressive acceleration. Researchers contest the self distilled checkpoint on

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:05.080
Sudoku or short form conditional tasks. Polestar uses token representation drift under bidirectional attention.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:10.320
It decides when to refresh KV cache entries and when to commit tokens.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:19.040
On math and coding benchmarks the approach delivers up to 10.73% accuracy gains and 3.7 times higher

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:26.540
throughput versus prior diffusion LLM baselines. It reaches 3.67 tokens per forward pass.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:33.620
The training-free method works across multiple diffusion LLM families, introspection fine tuning

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:40.760
fine tunes models on their own perturbed forward passes. Tasks include sentence localization and

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:50.400
strength comparison. Lama 1 billion accuracy on localization rises from 9.6% to 60.6% after the fine

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:56.620
tuning. The method generalizes to the held out strength task with negligible degradation on

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:05.000
standard capability benchmarks. T5 CS boost keeps the original T5 next token objective. It adds a

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:10.800
margin-based triplet loss on decoder embeddings. The model reaches state-of-the-art multi-class

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:19.580
attribution and human versus LLM detection on open LLM text and HC3. It shows strong robustness

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:25.620
to 90% intensity word and character level perturbations on the mage and deep fake suite.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:31.340
Q raised $5 million to scale its autonomous AI customer service agents.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:38.160
The Cape Town startup is expanding across the UK and South Africa. The agents operate without

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:43.960
human handoff and targeted verticals. Early traction centers on high-volume support workflows

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:50.700
where full autonomy reduces cost per ticket. Open AI shared details on its racing collaboration.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:57.720
Joyce Ruffel and race tech systems discuss turning track data into faster decisions with chat GPT

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:03.820
and codex. The work builds on an earlier research collaboration with Chip Gnassy Racing.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:10.720
Small margins in racing map directly to agentic tool use patterns where rapid iteration on structured

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:16.500
data matters. Key bank analysts flagged weak customer adoption of Salesforce agent force.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:22.720
The critique centers on deployment friction and unclear return on investment for enterprise buyers.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:29.040
Teams evaluating autonomous agent platforms should compare current capabilities against narrower

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:36.360
tools before committing. Crowd strikes field CTO warned that compromised AI agents could amplify

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:42.780
living off the land attacks. The concern centers on agents that already hold broad system access.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:49.400
Security teams running agentic workflows should add explicit tool use auditing and least privilege

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:58.040
scoping now. The EU AI Act Open Rag data set contains 933 legally structured chunks of regulation

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:06.880
EU 2024 over 1689. Chunks follow the regulations native structure of articles, recitals, definitions

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:16.260
and annexes. Structural chunking improved recall at 20-0.541 versus 0.449 for a baseline.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:26.080
Legal NLP and compliance teams can download the SQLite file with BGE-M3 embeddings for immediate rag

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:32.680
experimentation. LBA builds an approximate distribution of high quality adversarial examples

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:38.400
by combining prior and posterior knowledge. It then samples from the resulting distribution

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:44.760
to generate candidates. The method was evaluated on six language models and four data sets.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:50.140
It outperforms prior state-of-the-art approaches across every reported metric.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:56.000
Outputs maintain greater semantic preservation compared with earlier hard label techniques.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:01.140
The sampling step lowers the query cost relative to exhaustive search methods.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:07.920
Researchers building robustness evaluations should test LBA on their current hard label setups.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:15.280
AGGOPS uses a prompt writer, LLM, solver LLM, and evolutionary loop.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:20.080
It generates guidelines from reference answers without manual engineering.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:27.820
The method recovers 15.5 to 81.7% of the performance loss to underspecified prompts.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.980
Recovery was measured across math, medical QA, and coding tasks.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:38.240
Existing task examples are converted directly into reusable guidelines.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:45.120
Teams struggling with prompt consistency on a fixed task should run AGGOPS on their reference set

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:52.000
this week. Okay, let's pop the hood on multi-agent cascades. Intermediate transformations between

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:57.860
agents systematically compress the semantic distinctions needed for accurate downstream decisions.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:04.320
In the Collector Evaluator Decider Pipeline, critical evaluation reduces label separability

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:10.580
by 41.7% in embedding space on fact checking, sentiment, and triage tasks.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:14.840
Simple identity pass-through preserves nearly all separation.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:19.160
Prompt-level regression explains 78% of the variance.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:25.800
When building multi-agent flows, measure inter-label separation in sentence-transformer space

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:29.640
after each stage rather than trusting final accuracy alone.

